WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:04.208
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:04.208 --> 00:00:05.746
I'm a little bit sick today

00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:07.063
it's been a really rough week

00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:09.386
but this is the last video
I need to make for the week

00:00:09.386 --> 00:00:11.236
so I'm going to bring everything I have

00:00:11.236 --> 00:00:14.995
to this final video as we
talk about the seven ways

00:00:14.995 --> 00:00:19.670
to get started in your
business with zero cash.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.253
(techno music)

00:00:27.913 --> 00:00:29.047
So one of the most common questions

00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:32.204
that I get asked on my stream,
in my emails, on twitter,

00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.136
on YouTube is how do I get started?

00:00:34.136 --> 00:00:35.287
I don't have any money.

00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:36.860
I don't have an investor.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.426
You need money to make money.

00:00:38.426 --> 00:00:39.708
You don't.

00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:44.626
I'm going to show you how to
do it in seven different ways,

00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:46.855
how you can make money
and start a business

00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:49.303
without any start-up cap.

00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:50.220
Here we go.

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:55.617
Okay so way number one is start a service.

00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.966
I think entrepreneurs should
always start at the service

00:00:57.966 --> 00:01:00.062
over a product whenever possible

00:01:00.062 --> 00:01:01.532
'cause it does a couple things.

00:01:01.532 --> 00:01:02.743
One, when you start the service,

00:01:02.743 --> 00:01:04.799
you don't need to invest into any gear,

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:07.081
you don't need products,
you don't need a location.

00:01:07.081 --> 00:01:08.715
You can go to your clients.

00:01:08.715 --> 00:01:11.191
You're investing your time,
your energy, your hustle,

00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:13.153
but you're not investing your dollars.

00:01:13.153 --> 00:01:15.791
So it's a great way to get
started and test something out

00:01:15.791 --> 00:01:17.483
before investing money into it

00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:19.892
and as you start making money
then you can put it back in.

00:01:19.892 --> 00:01:21.339
So start with a service.

00:01:21.339 --> 00:01:23.280
The other thing that it
does with a service is

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.828
that it gets you close to your customers.

00:01:24.828 --> 00:01:25.883
When you're selling a product,

00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:27.352
you're not as close to your customer

00:01:27.352 --> 00:01:28.584
but when you're doing a service

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:30.970
and you're meeting with
them, whether it's every week

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.933
or every month or every
quarter, whatever it is.

00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:34.528
You're getting close to them ,

00:01:34.528 --> 00:01:36.058
you're getting to understand them.

00:01:36.058 --> 00:01:37.696
So you're getting their
money which is great,

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:39.441
you get cash still coming in without

00:01:39.441 --> 00:01:42.189
spending anything and
you're getting close to them

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:43.473
so you can understand their needs

00:01:43.473 --> 00:01:46.589
and when you're ready to make
the jump and sell product,

00:01:46.589 --> 00:01:49.096
you have a ready base already there.

00:01:49.096 --> 00:01:50.826
So you can get that attachment to them

00:01:50.826 --> 00:01:52.421
and when you're ready to go bigger,

00:01:52.421 --> 00:01:55.838
you already have that base to build from.

00:01:57.058 --> 00:01:59.929
Number two is use a
print on demand service.

00:01:59.929 --> 00:02:01.706
If you are going to any kind of product

00:02:01.706 --> 00:02:03.994
make sure that it's a
limited production run

00:02:03.994 --> 00:02:06.574
and that you're not
outlaying tons of cash.

00:02:06.574 --> 00:02:09.814
This is a big mistake that
a lot of entrepreneurs

00:02:09.814 --> 00:02:11.332
will make when they're
first getting started.

00:02:11.332 --> 00:02:13.622
If you want to make caps, right.

00:02:13.622 --> 00:02:16.532
I'm going to make caps, I want
to be in the cap making business.

00:02:16.532 --> 00:02:19.248
Great I've got this sick design
that's going to take off.

00:02:19.248 --> 00:02:20.652
Awesome.

00:02:20.652 --> 00:02:23.398
If you want to make real
margin off of baseball hats,

00:02:23.398 --> 00:02:26.411
you need to order tons, right,
you need to have 10,000.

00:02:26.411 --> 00:02:28.817
You need to order 5000, 10,000.

00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:31.895
The challenge is one that
costs a lot of money,

00:02:31.895 --> 00:02:33.262
you're going to have
to take out a big loan

00:02:33.262 --> 00:02:34.851
or take a mortgage on your house

00:02:34.851 --> 00:02:36.361
or sell everything you have.

00:02:36.361 --> 00:02:38.396
To get the start-up capital to be able

00:02:38.396 --> 00:02:40.350
to make the initial purchase.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.489
But the problem is you don't know

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:43.457
if that's going to sell or not.

00:02:43.457 --> 00:02:46.267
And it happens to so many people,
they go for the bulk order

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.080
'cause they get the biggest price breaks

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.973
and you figure if I can
sell all 10,000 of these,

00:02:50.973 --> 00:02:54.186
I'm going to make it rich, great.

00:02:54.186 --> 00:02:56.082
And then you sell three.

00:02:56.082 --> 00:02:58.648
Because maybe your design sucks,

00:02:58.648 --> 00:03:00.649
because maybe you wouldn't like it enough.

00:03:00.649 --> 00:03:04.783
And so I would much rather you
use a print on demand service

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.212
where you are selling one hat at a time

00:03:07.212 --> 00:03:09.153
and they're being
printed one hat at a time

00:03:09.153 --> 00:03:11.524
and being shipped one hat at a time

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.434
And there's services
that allow you to do this

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.112
for a huge range of products.

00:03:15.112 --> 00:03:16.952
Whatever you're tryin'
to get out there and sell

00:03:16.952 --> 00:03:19.903
and why it's great is you're
not spending any money.

00:03:19.903 --> 00:03:21.823
The downside is you're
not making as much money,

00:03:21.823 --> 00:03:24.290
right, where if you buy 10,00 caps,

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.435
you might be making a 90% margin.

00:03:26.435 --> 00:03:28.060
Where if you're selling one cap at a time,

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.432
you may be making 5% or 10%,
you're not making as much

00:03:31.432 --> 00:03:35.196
but what it allows you to do is test.

00:03:35.196 --> 00:03:38.317
What I would love to see you
do if you're going into caps

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:40.306
or t-shirts, whatever
you're trying to make,

00:03:40.306 --> 00:03:43.529
test your concept, see if it works,

00:03:43.529 --> 00:03:45.581
see if people want to buy it or not.

00:03:45.581 --> 00:03:48.321
And if you're selling these caps

00:03:48.321 --> 00:03:50.996
and your selling hundreds
and hundreds of caps,

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:52.331
then you can say you know what,

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.371
forget this print on demand service,

00:03:54.371 --> 00:03:56.002
I'm going to take the
money that I made from this

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.234
and I'm going to make my own order.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.319
Now it's worth it.

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:01.888
It's not risky because you
already have a ready audience.

00:04:01.888 --> 00:04:03.322
You know those are going to keep selling

00:04:03.322 --> 00:04:05.613
so use the print on
demand service to start,

00:04:05.613 --> 00:04:08.341
to test it, to build up an audience,

00:04:08.341 --> 00:04:11.012
and then when you're ready, make the jump.

00:04:11.012 --> 00:04:12.021
'Cause what I don't want you to do

00:04:12.021 --> 00:04:13.383
is take out a big mortgage

00:04:13.383 --> 00:04:16.216
and then get stuck with 9992 caps,

00:04:17.581 --> 00:04:20.224
sittin' in your mama's basement,

00:04:20.224 --> 00:04:23.346
'cause you couldn't sell
them and you took your shot

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:24.957
and now you're in debt
for the rest of your life.

00:04:24.957 --> 00:04:26.419
Don't do that.

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:28.919
Use a print on demand service.

00:04:31.242 --> 00:04:34.434
Number three is barter and borrow.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.821
Listen as an entrepreneur it's never

00:04:36.821 --> 00:04:38.881
about the resources you have,

00:04:38.881 --> 00:04:42.014
it's always about how
resourceful you can be

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:44.170
and so think about what you can barter,

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:45.497
think about what you can trade,

00:04:45.497 --> 00:04:46.944
think about what you're really good at

00:04:46.944 --> 00:04:49.225
and what you need help with
and maybe you could trade

00:04:49.225 --> 00:04:52.400
what you're really good
at with somebody else

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.735
'cause they need help with that.

00:04:53.735 --> 00:04:55.383
If you're lawyer trying to get started

00:04:55.383 --> 00:04:56.397
but you need a website,

00:04:56.397 --> 00:04:59.416
trade some legal services
to a website designer.

00:04:59.416 --> 00:05:01.770
They'll build you a website,
you got your legal services.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:05.536
Whatever it is, there's
people who need what you have,

00:05:05.536 --> 00:05:08.677
and you need what they have
so find some way to barter.

00:05:08.677 --> 00:05:11.706
As an example, after I
sold my first business,

00:05:11.706 --> 00:05:14.517
I needed a new office, I
needed a new thing to do

00:05:14.517 --> 00:05:17.113
and so I connected with
a venture capital company

00:05:17.113 --> 00:05:19.658
and they had this amazing
office at Yonge and King,

00:05:19.658 --> 00:05:20.491
which in Toronto,

00:05:20.491 --> 00:05:23.530
is one of the most prestigious
addresses you can have

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.659
pretty much in the country
actually, in Canada

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.964
and I was there and I
got the space for free

00:05:28.964 --> 00:05:31.440
and I got to incubate my
next company out of there

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.820
because I was able to
barter with the people

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.483
who owned that business.

00:05:35.483 --> 00:05:37.313
I joined them, I helped
them bring in deals

00:05:37.313 --> 00:05:40.022
at the same time I got to
incubate my business out of it

00:05:40.022 --> 00:05:42.180
and so look for people
who have what you need

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.649
and how you might be able
to work some kind of trade.

00:05:44.649 --> 00:05:46.770
The other thing is to
borrow, before you go out

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:50.105
and buy something, borrow from somebody.

00:05:50.105 --> 00:05:52.618
You get a landscaping deal great

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.293
but your first gig don't go
out and buy all the gear,

00:05:55.293 --> 00:05:57.536
go borrow the gear from
one of your friends

00:05:57.536 --> 00:05:59.768
that's sittin' in their garage
and they're not using it.

00:05:59.768 --> 00:06:01.969
When I was gettin' started on YouTube,

00:06:01.969 --> 00:06:04.630
I did both, I did barter and I did borrow.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.857
I had a friend of mine Mark Drager,

00:06:07.857 --> 00:06:09.865
who's actually featured in Your One Word

00:06:09.865 --> 00:06:11.848
was startin' at this
company Phantom Media,

00:06:11.848 --> 00:06:14.421
he came in and in exchange for promotion

00:06:14.421 --> 00:06:17.186
on the channel, he filmed my videos.

00:06:17.186 --> 00:06:20.062
So some of my very first
videos has this intro,

00:06:20.062 --> 00:06:22.952
created by Phantom Media or in association

00:06:22.952 --> 00:06:24.807
with Phantom Media, whatever it is,

00:06:24.807 --> 00:06:26.740
he got a lot of exposure on my channel

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.099
and in exchange he did
the video production

00:06:29.099 --> 00:06:32.849
and I was just the guy
in front of the camera

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:35.842
and so that was a great exchange,

00:06:35.842 --> 00:06:37.720
as I wanted to go off and do it myself,

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.248
the next step before I bought a camera

00:06:39.248 --> 00:06:41.979
was I borrowed a camera
from a buddy of mine.

00:06:41.979 --> 00:06:45.408
He was a bartender and
he did bartending tricks

00:06:45.408 --> 00:06:47.958
and flare and he filmed a
whole bunch of his events

00:06:47.958 --> 00:06:49.903
and I said hey can I borrow your camera?

00:06:49.903 --> 00:06:50.855
Would you mind, I want to make

00:06:50.855 --> 00:06:53.679
my own YouTube channel
videos and see what happens

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.222
and I borrowed his camera for a day.

00:06:55.222 --> 00:06:58.357
Borrow don't go and buy yet, borrow, test,

00:06:58.357 --> 00:07:00.707
always find a smaller way to get started.

00:07:00.707 --> 00:07:03.424
In almost any industry there's
a smaller way to get started.

00:07:03.424 --> 00:07:07.368
Go out and find that and then
pour it into your business.

00:07:07.368 --> 00:07:09.190
You look at Toronto Dance Salsa,

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.083
yes I have a retail location now.

00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:15.572
Yes it cost me six
figures in rent every year

00:07:15.572 --> 00:07:17.424
but how the business was started

00:07:17.424 --> 00:07:20.029
was renting spots out of gyms

00:07:20.029 --> 00:07:23.777
where we would pay 25,
30, 40 dollars an hour

00:07:23.777 --> 00:07:26.778
to rent their gym space for an hour

00:07:26.778 --> 00:07:30.207
and then fill it with students
and then we did more time,

00:07:30.207 --> 00:07:32.979
two hours, three hours at a
time and then multiple days.

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:35.897
If you want to start a bake
shop, you don't have to go out

00:07:35.897 --> 00:07:39.649
and take a five to ten
year lease on a bake shop.

00:07:39.649 --> 00:07:42.271
Find somebody who already
has some retail location

00:07:42.271 --> 00:07:46.139
and ask if you can have a
tiny part of their store.

00:07:46.139 --> 00:07:49.128
Come in for one day or come
in for everyday for a week,

00:07:49.128 --> 00:07:52.083
come in for every Saturday for a year,

00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:54.317
they take a piece of
every sale that comes in

00:07:54.317 --> 00:07:56.133
or whether they like it
for just the marketing

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:57.131
'cause you're bringing in awareness

00:07:57.131 --> 00:07:58.269
and people to the store.

00:07:58.269 --> 00:08:01.850
There's always a smaller
way to get started.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:05.815
Borrow, barter, think
smaller, think bigger

00:08:05.815 --> 00:08:08.707
at the same time, big goal, crunch it down

00:08:08.707 --> 00:08:10.941
into the next immediate
steps, because what happens,

00:08:10.941 --> 00:08:14.640
happens to a lot of you,
you have this big goal

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.191
and you think you have to
take this huge giant step,

00:08:17.191 --> 00:08:20.082
that's my next step, I
got to open up my store,

00:08:20.082 --> 00:08:21.555
that's my next step, I got
to take that big order,

00:08:21.555 --> 00:08:23.551
that's my next step
and then you do nothing

00:08:23.551 --> 00:08:24.944
because you can't get the capital

00:08:24.944 --> 00:08:27.343
and so you stay here at the
bottom having done nothing,

00:08:27.343 --> 00:08:29.718
and then years and years and years go by

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:32.176
and you see other people
makin' tons of cash

00:08:32.176 --> 00:08:34.554
off of your idea and you
freak out and complain

00:08:34.554 --> 00:08:35.753
and say that was my idea,

00:08:35.753 --> 00:08:38.337
I should be the one
making money off of that.

00:08:38.337 --> 00:08:40.366
No 'cause you didn't take any action.

00:08:40.366 --> 00:08:42.290
'Cause the idea alone is not enough,

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.645
you got to do the work

00:08:43.645 --> 00:08:45.432
and so stop tryin' to take that big step

00:08:45.432 --> 00:08:47.763
and instead doing nothing,

00:08:47.763 --> 00:08:50.234
small steps will lead to that big step.

00:08:50.234 --> 00:08:52.380
There is always a smaller
way to get started,

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:55.255
go find it and stop making excuses.

00:08:55.255 --> 00:08:56.755
Barter and borrow.

00:09:00.303 --> 00:09:02.940
Number four is pre-sell
and the idea here is,

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.464
use services like Kickstarter
or use an email list

00:09:06.464 --> 00:09:08.349
or use Facebook or whatever it is

00:09:08.349 --> 00:09:10.798
and start to pre-sell your idea.

00:09:10.798 --> 00:09:12.361
Whatever product, whatever service,

00:09:12.361 --> 00:09:13.922
whatever you have in your mind

00:09:13.922 --> 00:09:17.032
that you think might cost
you $10,000 or $50,000

00:09:17.032 --> 00:09:19.480
or whatever it is you think
it's going to cost you,

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.280
make a video about it,
make a web page about it,

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:23.560
you can do it yourself,

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.072
it doesn't have to cost you money,

00:09:25.072 --> 00:09:26.594
you're partnering with people
to help make that happen,

00:09:26.594 --> 00:09:28.803
and pre-sell it so before
you actually go out

00:09:28.803 --> 00:09:31.364
and write that book or before you go out

00:09:31.364 --> 00:09:33.921
and make that t-shirt,
or before you go out

00:09:33.921 --> 00:09:37.225
and launch that service,
you can pre-sell it

00:09:37.225 --> 00:09:39.350
and see if people are willing to buy it

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.139
and actually put money
down and say listen,

00:09:41.139 --> 00:09:45.547
if I get a hundred people who
will want to buy this book,

00:09:45.547 --> 00:09:48.207
I am going to write it
and here's the topic.

00:09:48.207 --> 00:09:49.920
If I get a thousand people,

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:53.087
who will pay for this specific e-book,

00:09:54.043 --> 00:09:55.540
then I'm going to write it.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.957
Or whatever it is, whatever
your product idea is,

00:09:57.957 --> 00:09:59.790
this new baseball hat,

00:10:01.543 --> 00:10:03.963
if I get 25 people to
commit to the first order

00:10:03.963 --> 00:10:06.026
of my baseball hat or a thousand people,

00:10:06.026 --> 00:10:08.260
whatever it is you need
to make your numbers work,

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.054
that's the whole point of Kickstarter,

00:10:10.054 --> 00:10:11.860
it's great 'cause you're
not givin' up equity.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.138
Remember when you're going to an investor,

00:10:13.138 --> 00:10:14.865
you're giving up equity in your business.

00:10:14.865 --> 00:10:17.063
Here it's just marketing,
if you don't hit the goal,

00:10:17.063 --> 00:10:18.407
you don't make the product.

00:10:18.407 --> 00:10:20.775
I mean it sucks, 'cause
you didn't make the goal,

00:10:20.775 --> 00:10:21.674
but it's great

00:10:21.674 --> 00:10:23.674
because you didn't outlay
thousands of dollars

00:10:23.674 --> 00:10:25.823
on this idea that's not going to take off.

00:10:25.823 --> 00:10:27.723
'Cause you don't have an audience for it

00:10:27.723 --> 00:10:30.471
so pre-selling is a
great, great, fantastic,

00:10:30.471 --> 00:10:33.745
amazing way to launch your business

00:10:33.745 --> 00:10:36.578
without having to spend any money.

00:10:38.199 --> 00:10:40.868
Number five is use free resources,

00:10:40.868 --> 00:10:44.380
just like bartering and
trading and borrowing,

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:45.502
I like free too.

00:10:45.502 --> 00:10:47.366
I like finding free ways to do stuff

00:10:47.366 --> 00:10:49.669
and so I would always look to free,

00:10:49.669 --> 00:10:51.733
even if it's not ideal,

00:10:51.733 --> 00:10:54.626
I would look to free before
paying for something.

00:10:54.626 --> 00:10:57.725
I want to start it, get
anything up, test it,

00:10:57.725 --> 00:10:59.363
and then as I start making some money,

00:10:59.363 --> 00:11:01.875
then I invest it back into growing.

00:11:01.875 --> 00:11:05.994
As an example there's this
great games cafe that opened up

00:11:05.994 --> 00:11:08.593
in Toronto where you pay
five to 10 dollars to get

00:11:08.593 --> 00:11:11.987
into the location and then you play games

00:11:11.987 --> 00:11:14.077
and then they sell food
and it's a coffee shop

00:11:14.077 --> 00:11:16.435
and it's a bar and they
have multiple locations now.

00:11:16.435 --> 00:11:19.075
When they started, it's
called Snakes and Lattes

00:11:19.075 --> 00:11:23.232
instead of Snakes and
Ladders, Snakes and Lattes.

00:11:23.232 --> 00:11:25.396
Anyway when they started,

00:11:25.396 --> 00:11:29.018
they didn't have a website,
instead of investing

00:11:29.018 --> 00:11:31.655
into a website they
just did it on Facebook.

00:11:31.655 --> 00:11:33.593
They did everything on Facebook.

00:11:33.593 --> 00:11:35.195
Facebook has all of the social connections

00:11:35.195 --> 00:11:37.660
all built in already ready to go.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:40.492
When you're starting you
don't need a website.

00:11:40.492 --> 00:11:41.439
Does it help you?

00:11:41.439 --> 00:11:43.040
Does it make you look more credible?

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.921
Does it allow you to do
more customized things?

00:11:45.921 --> 00:11:47.153
A hundred percent.

00:11:47.153 --> 00:11:48.938
But you don't need it.

00:11:48.938 --> 00:11:52.277
Start on Facebook just
start get something up.

00:11:52.277 --> 00:11:54.540
Get some attention, get some traction,

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.750
get your first dollars in

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.206
and then once you start making some money,

00:11:58.206 --> 00:12:00.684
you can figure out okay where
am I going to spend that?

00:12:00.684 --> 00:12:02.675
I'm going to spend that
on improving my product,

00:12:02.675 --> 00:12:04.167
I'm going to spend that on business cards,

00:12:04.167 --> 00:12:06.415
I'm going to spend it on an office car.

00:12:06.415 --> 00:12:07.893
Am I going to spend it on a new website?

00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:09.322
Where am I going to spend it?

00:12:09.322 --> 00:12:11.244
When you're meeting people
you don't need an office

00:12:11.244 --> 00:12:15.426
Having an office should never
be anything you consider

00:12:15.426 --> 00:12:16.830
until you're making some money.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.617
Meet people at their location.

00:12:18.617 --> 00:12:20.373
Meet people in Starbucks.

00:12:20.373 --> 00:12:22.498
I still meet people at Starbucks.

00:12:22.498 --> 00:12:23.791
I like getting out of the office.

00:12:23.791 --> 00:12:24.950
You don't need to have an office.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:26.891
Stop finding ways to spend money,

00:12:26.891 --> 00:12:28.233
anybody can spend money,

00:12:28.233 --> 00:12:29.473
anybody can put a budget together

00:12:29.473 --> 00:12:31.344
and say hey I need a million
dollars to go and do this

00:12:31.344 --> 00:12:32.504
and here's how we're going to spend it.

00:12:32.504 --> 00:12:33.520
Amazing.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.505
I'm sure you could find millions of ways

00:12:35.505 --> 00:12:37.933
to spend a million dollars,
you'll figure it out.

00:12:37.933 --> 00:12:38.950
Anybody can spend money.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.440
Not everybody can make it.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:44.107
So find ways to go free
like using Facebook,

00:12:45.285 --> 00:12:46.923
like not having a business card,

00:12:46.923 --> 00:12:50.699
like not buying office
equipment, any of that stuff,

00:12:50.699 --> 00:12:54.866
go to coffee shops until
you're making some money.

00:12:57.381 --> 00:13:00.811
Number six is turn your job into a client.

00:13:00.811 --> 00:13:02.876
I've always been a big
proponent of if you're

00:13:02.876 --> 00:13:04.073
going to have a job,

00:13:04.073 --> 00:13:07.513
don't look at it as just
having an income source,

00:13:07.513 --> 00:13:08.925
yes you need to make money and it's great.

00:13:08.925 --> 00:13:11.239
You need to be learning from your job,

00:13:11.239 --> 00:13:13.981
the point of taking a job is to learn,

00:13:13.981 --> 00:13:16.509
so whatever business you want to get into,

00:13:16.509 --> 00:13:18.270
whatever this new company
you want to start,

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:19.830
the ideal scenario is
to find somebody who's

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.532
already done that and go work for them.

00:13:21.532 --> 00:13:23.839
Find somebody who has 10 employees,

00:13:23.839 --> 00:13:26.651
some small company whose
built up, is bigger than you

00:13:26.651 --> 00:13:28.637
but not some giant where
the job you're going to get

00:13:28.637 --> 00:13:31.007
is tiny and not helpful

00:13:31.007 --> 00:13:33.117
and then go work for them to learn.

00:13:33.117 --> 00:13:35.277
Yes get paid but to learn.

00:13:35.277 --> 00:13:39.667
So how do you transition
that job into a business?

00:13:39.667 --> 00:13:41.534
The two things that come to mind are one,

00:13:41.534 --> 00:13:42.908
that company that you're working for

00:13:42.908 --> 00:13:44.641
could become your first client.

00:13:44.641 --> 00:13:45.550
It happens a lot,

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.538
where you need to free
up some on your time,

00:13:47.538 --> 00:13:49.502
you don't want to be an employee anymore

00:13:49.502 --> 00:13:51.926
and so you become an
independent contractor

00:13:51.926 --> 00:13:54.035
where instead of going
to work five days a week,

00:13:54.035 --> 00:13:57.181
you work three days a
week or two days a week

00:13:57.181 --> 00:13:58.528
or one day a week,

00:13:58.528 --> 00:14:00.027
and maybe it's not from
the office anymore,

00:14:00.027 --> 00:14:02.621
maybe you work from home
and you're not an employee,

00:14:02.621 --> 00:14:05.162
with the benefits and
all the taxes anymore,

00:14:05.162 --> 00:14:08.433
you're an independent contractor
running your own company

00:14:08.433 --> 00:14:10.719
and so it gives you some money,

00:14:10.719 --> 00:14:13.334
it gives you your own client
and you're in business.

00:14:13.334 --> 00:14:15.999
The second way to do it is to
use some of the opportunities

00:14:15.999 --> 00:14:18.992
that come through this
business that you're working at

00:14:18.992 --> 00:14:20.872
for your own advantage.

00:14:20.872 --> 00:14:22.883
So you might be able to
take one of the clients

00:14:22.883 --> 00:14:23.833
that you're working on

00:14:23.833 --> 00:14:25.370
or you meet somebody at a networking event

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.836
because you're going there,
you're forming contacts,

00:14:27.836 --> 00:14:29.474
you're forming partnerships,

00:14:29.474 --> 00:14:32.149
by being in the space you
get to make connections.

00:14:32.149 --> 00:14:34.828
You may see an opportunity for,

00:14:34.828 --> 00:14:36.797
you go to this networking
event and there's this person

00:14:36.797 --> 00:14:39.098
that you meet and there's
an opportunity for you

00:14:39.098 --> 00:14:41.555
to work with them, for
them to be your client.

00:14:41.555 --> 00:14:42.762
So you bring them on board

00:14:42.762 --> 00:14:44.655
and that could be your
first client as well.

00:14:44.655 --> 00:14:47.116
Either from becoming an
independent contractor

00:14:47.116 --> 00:14:48.642
and splitting up your week,

00:14:48.642 --> 00:14:50.603
so you're not spending
full time at your job

00:14:50.603 --> 00:14:54.608
or using the connections that you build

00:14:54.608 --> 00:14:56.277
which is why it's so
important to have a job

00:14:56.277 --> 00:14:59.723
in the industry that you want
to build your business in,

00:14:59.723 --> 00:15:02.376
you're making contacts and
from there one of those

00:15:02.376 --> 00:15:04.459
become your first client.

00:15:07.008 --> 00:15:09.564
And the number seven and
final way to build a business

00:15:09.564 --> 00:15:11.946
without having to spend any cash,

00:15:11.946 --> 00:15:14.185
and it's an important one,

00:15:14.185 --> 00:15:16.185
build around a customer.

00:15:17.361 --> 00:15:18.708
Business is about providing value

00:15:18.708 --> 00:15:21.209
and I've talked a lot, a
lot, a lot, a lot, a lot,

00:15:21.209 --> 00:15:23.392
about this on this channel
if you want to make money,

00:15:23.392 --> 00:15:25.746
you have to provide value to your clients.

00:15:25.746 --> 00:15:29.024
Having success in
business is going to come

00:15:29.024 --> 00:15:30.691
from combining two things,

00:15:30.691 --> 00:15:32.762
this is how you're going to provide value,

00:15:32.762 --> 00:15:36.240
in this corner, in this
fist is what you love doing.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.013
This is your passion, this
is what you love doing

00:15:39.013 --> 00:15:42.481
and in this corner, in this
fist is what the market wants,

00:15:42.481 --> 00:15:44.404
what your clients want,

00:15:44.404 --> 00:15:47.754
your success will come by
bringing these two together

00:15:47.754 --> 00:15:50.047
because if you love doing something

00:15:50.047 --> 00:15:52.164
but it provides no value to anybody else,

00:15:52.164 --> 00:15:55.360
it's going to be a hard time
becoming a successful entrepreneur

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:58.119
and if all you're doing
is chasing opportunity,

00:15:58.119 --> 00:15:59.727
but you're not interested in it,

00:15:59.727 --> 00:16:01.472
you're never going to really be a success,

00:16:01.472 --> 00:16:03.312
you may make a few bucks but
you're never going to really

00:16:03.312 --> 00:16:04.637
be a successful entrepreneur.

00:16:04.637 --> 00:16:07.478
So you need to combine what you love doing

00:16:07.478 --> 00:16:10.602
with what people will pay
for with the market wants.

00:16:10.602 --> 00:16:13.210
There's been a ton of video
series that I've put up

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.975
that I love doing but you
guys didn't resonate with

00:16:15.975 --> 00:16:18.115
and that I pulled down.

00:16:18.115 --> 00:16:20.542
Some I do keep up but recognize

00:16:20.542 --> 00:16:23.174
that this is really just for me

00:16:23.174 --> 00:16:25.094
but if I had to build my
whole channel around it,

00:16:25.094 --> 00:16:25.941
it wouldn't work.

00:16:25.941 --> 00:16:28.369
There's been other ones
that I could easily go to,

00:16:28.369 --> 00:16:32.536
if I put 10 stupidest things
that Steve Jobs ever said,

00:16:35.778 --> 00:16:38.904
10 biggest fights with Donald Trump,

00:16:38.904 --> 00:16:41.155
if I started doing those kinds of videos,

00:16:41.155 --> 00:16:42.734
people would eat that up,

00:16:42.734 --> 00:16:45.760
they might be the most
popular videos on my channel,

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.891
people would love that

00:16:47.891 --> 00:16:49.406
but the idea of putting people down

00:16:49.406 --> 00:16:51.680
and making people look stupid,

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:54.846
and just causing controversy
for the sake of fighting,

00:16:54.846 --> 00:16:56.345
I don't like it at all.

00:16:56.345 --> 00:16:59.388
I never want to do that stuff
it's not part of who I am

00:16:59.388 --> 00:17:01.674
and so I'm not making
those videos even though

00:17:01.674 --> 00:17:03.745
there is a demand because other people

00:17:03.745 --> 00:17:06.091
would do a better job
at it anyway then me.

00:17:06.091 --> 00:17:07.639
I don't want to play in that game.

00:17:07.639 --> 00:17:10.189
And so combining what you love

00:17:10.189 --> 00:17:13.124
with what the market
wants is super important

00:17:13.124 --> 00:17:16.944
and that's why you need to get
close to potential customers

00:17:16.944 --> 00:17:20.143
and build a product or service around them

00:17:20.143 --> 00:17:23.560
so instead of just saying here's my idea,

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:27.202
go buy or don't buy.

00:17:27.202 --> 00:17:28.818
Be more collaborative.

00:17:28.818 --> 00:17:30.621
Think about who potential customers

00:17:30.621 --> 00:17:33.632
would be for your service
of for your product

00:17:33.632 --> 00:17:36.574
and go out and talk to them
ask them what they think,

00:17:36.574 --> 00:17:38.083
ask them what their needs are,

00:17:38.083 --> 00:17:39.180
ask them what their problems are,

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.310
ask them what their pains are

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:44.124
if I made this for you, or
I came and did this for you

00:17:44.124 --> 00:17:47.196
would it help would that be
something that you would pay for

00:17:47.196 --> 00:17:48.765
is that enough value for you?

00:17:48.765 --> 00:17:52.674
If you get a yes and it's work
that you would want to do,

00:17:52.674 --> 00:17:55.137
then you're in business and If not

00:17:55.137 --> 00:17:56.923
then you need to keep talking to people,

00:17:56.923 --> 00:17:58.135
keep meeting people, make a list

00:17:58.135 --> 00:17:59.794
of all the potential customers,

00:17:59.794 --> 00:18:02.321
these are the kinds of
people who would buy from me

00:18:02.321 --> 00:18:03.924
and go understand them.

00:18:03.924 --> 00:18:05.871
So instead of just selling them something,

00:18:05.871 --> 00:18:08.699
instead of just saying here
is a solution for you ,

00:18:08.699 --> 00:18:12.623
it's talking to them and
building a business around them.

00:18:12.623 --> 00:18:15.465
This is something I did really
in my very first business,

00:18:15.465 --> 00:18:18.922
even in this business, look the top 10's,

00:18:18.922 --> 00:18:22.423
most of the videos that
we make on this channel

00:18:22.423 --> 00:18:25.677
are your requests, like what
do you guys want to hear?

00:18:25.677 --> 00:18:27.688
Who do you guys want
us to make a video on?

00:18:27.688 --> 00:18:29.858
What topic do you want to hear from?

00:18:29.858 --> 00:18:32.445
We collect it, we think
about, we pick the ones

00:18:32.445 --> 00:18:35.283
that we like the most too and
then we start running with it.

00:18:35.283 --> 00:18:38.429
In my first business, the
biotech software company,

00:18:38.429 --> 00:18:40.519
all of the features that we built ended up

00:18:40.519 --> 00:18:43.303
being around what are customer's wanted.

00:18:43.303 --> 00:18:45.896
You know you want this
thing added to the software,

00:18:45.896 --> 00:18:49.422
great it's going to cost you
this amount of money to do it.

00:18:49.422 --> 00:18:51.453
And then we roll that
feature into the software

00:18:51.453 --> 00:18:53.072
for everybody else as well,

00:18:53.072 --> 00:18:56.129
to get some custom development,
we're not out money

00:18:56.129 --> 00:18:57.861
on the development,

00:18:57.861 --> 00:19:00.153
and then we can roll it out
for everybody else as well.

00:19:00.153 --> 00:19:01.760
You want it translated into Spanish?

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.721
Perfect it's going to cost
this amount of money to do it,

00:19:04.721 --> 00:19:07.507
provides enough value to
them even if that alone

00:19:07.507 --> 00:19:08.764
is break even,

00:19:08.764 --> 00:19:10.557
even if you're not making
a profit off of that,

00:19:10.557 --> 00:19:12.803
we can roll it out to everybody else

00:19:12.803 --> 00:19:14.294
and add more value to them.

00:19:14.294 --> 00:19:19.038
Building your business around
a customer is so, so, so, so

00:19:19.038 --> 00:19:20.975
important especially in the early days.

00:19:20.975 --> 00:19:23.911
So those are my seven ways
on how to start a business

00:19:23.911 --> 00:19:25.525
without having any cash.

00:19:25.525 --> 00:19:27.842
I'm curious what do you guys think?

00:19:27.842 --> 00:19:29.380
What was you favorite rule?

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:30.728
What resonated the most with you?

00:19:30.728 --> 00:19:32.093
What are you going to
take from this and apply

00:19:32.093 --> 00:19:34.304
to your business immediately?

00:19:34.304 --> 00:19:35.942
Did I miss something that you want to add?

00:19:35.942 --> 00:19:38.762
Is there eight, nine, 10 that
you want to add to the list?

00:19:38.762 --> 00:19:41.076
Leave it down in the comments below.

